# The copy the cipher trigger makes is cast during the trigger's resolution (CR 702.99a, 707.12), so what forbids casting a spell
# forbids it: it is Bot2's own Trait Doctoring, encoded on Bot2's Llanowar Elves. On turn 4 the Elves connect and, with no
# Teferi out, Bot2 is offered the copy and casts it (the positive control). Bot1's Teferi, Time Raveler ("each opponent can
# cast spells only any time they could cast a sorcery", CR 307.1) comes down on turn 5; on turn 6 the Elves connect with the
# trigger on the stack, which is not a time Bot2 could cast a sorcery, so the trigger resolves and offers nothing (the ruling:
# if you can't cast the copy you don't, and it ceases to exist). The card is still encoded and exiled (CR 702.99c).

